description:
The alphabet is split per Unicode codepoint, so multibyte alphabets work;
duplicate characters are collapsed. Length is chosen uniformly within an
inclusive range.

```php
#[Property(runs: 500)]
public function holds(int $n): void
{
    Classify::when($n === 0, 'zero');
    Classify::when($n < 0, 'negative');
    Classify::label($n % 2 === 0 ? 'even' : 'odd');
    // ... assertions ...
}
```

After a fully passing property the runner prints the share of runs that hit
each label. A label recorded several times within one run still counts once
for that run.

State is per-run and process-local: the runner clears it before each run via
\Rasuvaeff\PropertyTesting\beginRun() and drains it via \Rasuvaeff\PropertyTesting\flushRun(). Property runs are
sequential, so the static buffer is never shared concurrently.

publicMethods.description:
```php
Classify::cover($n % 2 === 0, 'even', 30.0);
```

summary:
The standalone executor: a plain callback is the property body. A normal
return passes, \Rasuvaeff\PropertyTesting\Assume::that() discards,
any other throwable fails the trial.
